{"text": "M. ALLISON MOORE\n(BB)\n\nPROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\nRepublican National Committee Washington, DC\nNational Press Secretary February 2015-present\n\u2018\u00a2 Primary press contact and on-the-record spokesperson for all national media inquiries.\n\u2018\u00a9 Dai collaborations with senior staf in all departments to identify opportunities and successfully sell positive news articles about the\nNC to national print and broadcast reporters.\n\u2018\u00a9 Manage state and regional press secretaries, as well as communicate intemal positions to members of the RNC and other surrogates\nto ensure consistent messaging across all mediums nationwide.\n\u2018* Responsible for briefing and staffing the Republican National Committee Chairman for national TV, radio and print interviews, press\nconferences, debates, and other high-profile media events.\n\u2018\u00a2 Played an integral role in developing and marketing budgeted media campaigns, which helped garner over a billion dollars in eamed\nmedia for the RNC over the 2016 election cycle.\n\u2018\u00a9 Worked closely with networks, vendors, and press to manage the planning, production, and credentialing for media fling centers at\nGOP Presidential Primary Debates.\n\nMcConnell Senate Committee, Re-Election Campaign \u201814 Louisville, KY\nPress Secretary \u2018August 2013 - December 2014\n\u2018\u00a9 Led the press operation for U.S. Senate Majority Leader Mitch McConnell\u2019 re-election campaign, which resulted in a 25 point victory\nin the primary election and a 16 point victory in the general election.\n\n\u2018\u00a9 Primary on-the-record spokesperson forall campaign communications.\n\u2018\u00a9 Successfully pitched hundreds of stories with local and national journalists in order to shape and drive the campaign's narratives.\n\u2018\u00a9 Traveled with Leader McConnell to campaign media events.\n\u2018\u00a9 Oversaw rapid response efforts during the debate and other high-profile media events throughout the campaign.\n\u2018\u00a2 Managed press assistants and delegated responsibilities as necessary o ensure maximum attendance and positive coverage of all\nmedia events,\nUnited States Senate, Senate Republican Communications Center Washington, DC\nBroadcast Communications Advisor March 2010 \u2014 August 2013\n\n\u2018* New position created by the Leaders ofice following consistently excellent performance reviews and senior staf feedback\n\u2018* Coordinated and managed all of Senate Republican Leader Mitch McConnell\u2019s national media appearances, including CBS\u2019 60\nMinutes and a special \u201cinside Congress\u201d edition of Dateline NBC.\n\u2018* Primary radio booking contact forall Republican senators.\n\u2018\u00a2 Developed lasting relationships with several hundred TV and radio hosts and producers nationwide inorder to orchestrate media\nappearances forall Republican senators.\n\u2018\u00a9 Assisted in crating and executing Republican media strategy by providing hosts/producers with daily updates and specific messaging\nangles crafted by the SRC.\n\u2018\u00a9 One of few staf chosen by Leader McConnell to travel to Kentucky to assist inthe final weeks of Sen. Rand Pau's election campaign\nin 2010,\n\nDeputy Press Secretary January 2008 March 2010\n\u2018\u00a9 Organized and executed two successful vitual radio rows within one week for al Republican senators, earning recognition in the\nradio industry's Talkers Magazine as a source for producers and hosts nationwide.\n\u00a9 Developed and maintained effective relationships while serving as the primary point of contact between the SRCC and alll radio\n\nmedia,\n\u2018* Provided radio hosts and producers across the country with daily updates, audio clips, and other information to assis n their\nbroadcasts.\nUnited States Senate, Office of the Senate Republican Leader \u2018Washington, DC\nStaff Assistant June 2007 = January 2008\n\n\u2018\u00a9 Greeted and attended to various groups, diplomats, and heads of state prior to meetings and events withthe Leader.\n\u2018\u00ae Communicated the Leader's positon to hundreds of constituents caling his leadership office on a daily basis.\nEDUCATION\n\nUniversity of Kentucky Lexington, KY\nBachelor of Arts, Political Science, May 2007",
